<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20527" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hērennĭus</span></b> , a,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a
				Roman</i> gens, e. g. C. Herennius, <i>to whom
			the</i> Rhetorica <i>of Cornificius is dedicated</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">M. Herennius,</span>”
				<i>an orator</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 45, 166</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Mur. 17, 36</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Herennius Gallus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					4, 13</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">26</span></i> sq.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Herennius Senecio,</span>”
				<i>a historian under Domitian</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. Agr.
				2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">45</span></i>; <i>a Samnite</i> Herennius,
				<i><span class="en">Liv. 9,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Flor. 1, 16,
			10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hērennĭānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a Herennius</i>, <i>Herennian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coheredes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 13, 6, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
